            <div xml:id="d68">

                <pb facs="0215" n="101" sameAs="frus:frus1931v01/pg101"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">462.00R296/4180: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Edge</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                    State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Paris</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1931-06-29T13:00:00+01:00">June 29, 1931—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received June 29—9:16 a.m.<anchor n="95" xml:id="d68-f1"
                        />]</dateline></opener>
                <p>372. The conference with the French Ministers lasted from 10:30 to 12:30. A net
                    result was a decision on the part of Monsieur Laval to call an emergency meeting
                    of the Council of Ministers at 6 tonight. We are to meet the conferees,
                    following a Council meeting at 9:30 tonight. I have already put in a telephone
                    call for the Acting Secretary for 10 a.m. Washington time.</p>
                <p>[Paraphrase.] We presented the President’s counterproposal as contained in your
                    telegram No. 298, June 27, 10 p.m., and as previously given to the Minister of
                    Finance (see Embassy’s 371, June 29, 1 a.m.). Although Monsieur Laval expressed
                    his doubt as to its being accepted, he agreed to present the counterproposal to
                    the Cabinet tonight.</p>
                <p>Following this discussion this direct question was asked by Laval: “What will
                    happen if the Council refuses to accept the counterproposal?” We then frankly
                    outlined the next step the President would probably take according to
                    Department’s telegram 298.</p>
                <p>It is understood that no statement would be published of this situation at this
                    time. [End paraphrase.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Edge</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
